    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), whose matchup against Tanner Bibee is our strongest play. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite park factor and a significant boost from a slow pitcher delivery, which elevates his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor for our roster\u2019s efficiency. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also represent high-leverage starts, both facing favorable matchups against arms with xERAs above 4.70. While **Kyle Tucker** (74.11) faces a tough southpaw in Nick Lodolo, his elite base projection keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start category, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.54) remains a high-floor anchor in the utility spot despite a slightly tougher matchup against Jack Perkins.\n\nWe are navigating a few \"Lineup Pending\" designations, adding volatility to our roster construction. **Henry Bolte** (58.98) and **Liam Hicks** (59.93) are hovering near the marginal threshold; while their park and platoon conditions are neutral to positive, they lack the multi-category upside of our top-tier starters. The most difficult decision rested on the bench, where **Tommy White** (53.21) was the final cut. While **Tommy White** benefited from a +10% park factor against Jos\u00e9 Soriano, his lower batting order projection relative to **Heliot Ramos** (64.32) relegated him to the bench. Similarly, **Nasim Nunez** (50.78) was sidelined primarily due to an unfavorable #9 spot in the lineup, despite his potential to impact the stolen base category should he find his way onto the basepaths.\n\nThe primary risk today remains the reliance on projected lineup positions. Because the official lineups are not yet posted, any drop in the order for players like **Drake Baldwin** or **Miguel Vargas** could drag their efficiency scores toward the 50s. We are keeping a close eye on the weather and confirmed lineups; if **Wade Meckler** (51.35) continues to struggle with a same-handed platoon disadvantage against Patrick Sandoval, we may shift our target for game-cap preservation. Every player currently starting is positioned to capitalize on soft opposing starters, but maintaining our competitive edge in stolen bases remains the priority as we deploy this high-efficiency group.",
